{title: Tar Pits and Treasures}
{subtitle: Genesis 14:1; 14:8–10; 14:11–12; 14:14–16}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [C] | [Dm] [C] |
| [Bb] [C] | [Dm] | ×5

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In days of Amraphel [C]king of Shinar
[Bb]Arioch ruled in Ella[C]sar
Chedor[Dm]laomer of Elam [C]stood
[Bb]Tidal king of [C]Goiim [Dm]led
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Four kings formed a [C]powerful band
A[Dm]gainst the five [C]in the land
[Dm]Sodom and Gomorrah [C]marched out
[Bb]Admah and Ze[C]boiim [Dm]fought
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Valley of Siddim [C]full of pits
[Dm]Tar rose up [Am]as the dust
[Bb]Kings of Sodom [C]fell inside
Go[Bb]morrah kings [C]could not [Dm]hide
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The victors seized [C]goods and food
Pro[Dm]visions taken [C]from the wood
[Dm]Lot was taken [C]from his home
[Bb]Abram heard the [C]sorrowing [Dm]tone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Three [Bb]hundred eighteen [C]men
[Dm]Born in his household [Am]when
[Bb]He pursued to [C]Dan and [Bb]far
North of Dam[C]ascus at [Dm]war
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] [C] | [Dm] [Am] | [Bb] [C] | [Dm] | ×4

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]He divided [C]his forces [Dm]at night
Attacked in [Am]the fading light
[Bb]Recovered [C]all the goods
[Bb]Brought Lot back [C]from the [Dm]crowds
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Women and [C]people re[Dm]stored
[Bb]Abram’s [C]story is re[Dm]corded
{end_of_verse}

